# Touch this file (any change) to run .github/workflows/apple-revoke-log.yml on
# the current branch, which is the only way to run it until that workflow
# reaches the default branch — GitHub lists workflow_dispatch workflows from
# there alone. The same device supabase/.deploy-request and
# .github/push-key-request use.
#
# The run only READS, and it prints a classification of each Apple log line
# rather than the line. The entry below is a prediction, written before the
# run, so that a run which disagrees with it is visible as a disagreement.

2026-09-04 — first run. The founder created an account with Sign in with Apple
             and deleted it, hours after run #105 synced the four APPLE_*
             function secrets. Expect one `apple revoke: ok (200)` from
             delete-account and no `store-apple-token:` lines at all, since
             that function logs nothing on success. Anything else is the
             interesting case: `no token for this account` would mean the
             sign-in never stored one, which is the false pass this doc has
             been warning about since the key was still missing.
